# Domains and service boundaries

| Domain | Railway service | Public |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `api.notorganic.info` | gateway | Yes |
| `id.notorganic.info` | portal | Yes |
| `pds.notorganic.info` | PDS | Yes |
| `openbao.railway.internal:8200` | OpenBao | No |

The gateway is the only public inference entry point. OpenBao must never receive
a Railway public domain. PDS account creation is invite-only and restricted to
`did:plc`; wildcard handle resolution uses `*.pds.notorganic.info` DNS only if
the PDS configuration requires it.

Health checks:

- Gateway: `GET /healthz` must validate process readiness without exposing keys.
- Portal: `GET /healthz`.
- PDS: `GET /xrpc/_health`.
- OpenBao: `GET /v1/sys/health?standbyok=true&sealedcode=200&uninitcode=200`.
# Operations runbook

## Railway services and secrets

Create four services from the service-specific Railway JSON files. Attach
persistent volumes at `/pds` (PDS) and `/openbao/data` (OpenBao). Keep OpenBao
private; `api`, `id`, and `pds` receive the public domains documented in
`domains.md`.

Required secret groups:

- Gateway: `CONVEX_URL`, the same 32+ byte `CONVEX_GATEWAY_SECRET` configured
  in Convex, Portkey credentials, provider signing JWKs and assertion public
  JWKs, `PROVIDER_PSEUDONYM_SECRET`, OpenBao AppRole credentials, Creem API
  key/catalog, model allowlists, and reconciliation-cost policy.
- Portal build: `VITE_PORTAL_API_URL=https://api.notorganic.info`.
- PDS: the official PDS secrets plus `R2_ENDPOINT`, `R2_BUCKET`,
  `R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, and `R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`. Set
  `PDS_HOSTNAME=pds.notorganic.info`,
  `PDS_DATA_DIRECTORY=/pds`, and disable open registration. Provision invites
  through the authenticated provider workflow only.
- OpenBao: a Railway secret named `BAO_AUTO_UNSEAL_KEY` containing 32 random
  bytes encoded as base64, plus no public domain.

Never put a Creem key, PDS admin token, OpenBao token, or signing key in a
`VITE_*` variable.

## OpenBao bootstrap

1. Deploy with an empty persistent volume and the Railway-held static auto-seal
   key already present.
2. From a private Railway shell run:
   `bao operator init -recovery-shares=5 -recovery-threshold=3`.
3. Distribute the five Shamir recovery shares to separate offline custodians;
   store none in Railway, source control, R2, or the snapshot bucket.
4. Use the initial root token once to enable audit logging and Transit:
   `bao secrets enable transit`, then
   `bao write -f transit/keys/provider-responses derived=true`.
5. Create a `provider-gateway` policy granting only
   `update` on `transit/encrypt/provider-responses`,
   `transit/decrypt/provider-responses`, and `auth/token/renew-self`.
   Enable AppRole with `bao auth enable approle`, create a
   `provider-gateway` role with that policy and a short token TTL, and put its
   role ID/secret ID in Railway as `OPENBAO_ROLE_ID`/`OPENBAO_SECRET_ID`.
   Revoke the initial root token. A static `OPENBAO_TOKEN` remains a
   break-glass/testing option, not the normal production configuration.
6. Confirm restart auto-unseals and `/v1/sys/health` reports initialized,
   unsealed, and active before storing production secrets.

The Railway auto-unseal key and three offline recovery shares are separate
failure domains. Losing the Railway key makes snapshots unrecoverable; losing
three recovery shares prevents administrative key rotation. Rotate the static
seal key using OpenBao's documented seal migration procedure, never by simply
replacing the environment value.

## Snapshots and restore drills

Run `infra/openbao/snapshot.sh` from a private scheduled job with a short-lived,
snapshot-only token and R2 credentials. Keep daily snapshots for 30 days and
monthly snapshots for one year using R2 lifecycle rules. Enable object
versioning and prevent the runtime credentials from deleting object versions.

Quarterly restore drill:

1. Create an isolated OpenBao service and fresh volume.
2. Supply the matching historical auto-unseal key.
3. Download a snapshot and run `bao operator raft snapshot restore -force`.
4. Verify unseal, audit devices, policies, and a synthetic secret read.
5. Destroy the isolated service and record recovery time and snapshot age.

Litestream continuously replicates PDS SQLite to R2. Before restoring, stop the
PDS service to avoid split-brain writes, restore the newest replica, start one
PDS replica, and verify repository and blob reads. PDS blobs use the dedicated
R2 bucket configured in PDS; SQLite replicas and OpenBao snapshots use distinct
prefixes and credentials.

## Incident controls

- Creem webhook failures: preserve raw delivery IDs in Creem, fix verification,
  then replay. Convex event IDs and object timestamps make replay idempotent and
  ignore stale subscription events.
- Stuck inference: the five-minute reservation sweep releases grants/cash.
- Gateway health: `/healthz` must verify both Convex and OpenBao; Railway
  should not route traffic to a dependency-degraded instance.
- OpenBao sealed: do not initialize again. Check the volume and auto-unseal key;
  restore from snapshot only after confirming the volume is unrecoverable.
- PDS deletion: provider-data and PDS-account deletion are independent,
  separately confirmed jobs. Never infer one from the other.
- Compromise: rotate provider signing keys, service principals, OpenBao AppRole
  secrets, PDS admin token, Creem keys, and R2 credentials; then invalidate
  affected sessions.
import { FormEvent, ReactNode, useState } from "react";
import { AccountStatus, AuditView, portalApi, VersionView } from "./api";

type View = "account" | "admin";

function Panel({ title, eyebrow, children }: { title: string; eyebrow: string; children: ReactNode }) {
  return (
    <section className="panel">
      <p className="eyebrow">{eyebrow}</p>
      <h2>{title}</h2>
      {children}
    </section>
  );
}

function useOperation() {
  const [message, setMessage] = useState("");
  const run = async (operation: () => Promise<unknown>, success: string) => {
    setMessage("Working…");
    try {
      await operation();
      setMessage(success);
    } catch (error) {
      setMessage(error instanceof Error ? error.message : "Request failed");
    }
  };
  return { message, run };
}

function AccountTools() {
  const invite = useOperation();
  const recovery = useOperation();
  const deletion = useOperation();

  const redeem = (event: FormEvent<HTMLFormElement>) => {
    event.preventDefault();
    const data = Object.fromEntries(new FormData(event.currentTarget).entries()) as Record<string, string>;
    void invite.run(() => portalApi.redeemInvite(data), "Invite redeemed. Your managed PDS account is connected.");
  };
  const recover = (event: FormEvent<HTMLFormElement>) => {
    event.preventDefault();
    const data = Object.fromEntries(new FormData(event.currentTarget).entries()) as Record<string, string>;
    void recovery.run(
      () => portalApi.completeRecovery({ challengeHash: data.challengeHash ?? "", newPdsUrl: data.newPdsUrl ?? "" }),
      "Recovery completed.",
    );
  };
  const exportData = async () => {
    const data = await portalApi.exportMine();
    const url = URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([JSON.stringify(data, null, 2)], { type: "application/json" }));
    const anchor = document.createElement("a");
    anchor.href = url;
    anchor.download = `notorganic-export-${new Date().toISOString()}.json`;
    anchor.click();
    URL.revokeObjectURL(url);
  };

  return (
    <div className="grid">
      <Panel eyebrow="Invite-only identity" title="Connect your did:plc">
        <form onSubmit={redeem}>
          <label>Invite token hash<input name="tokenHash" required /></label>
          <label>DID<input name="did" required pattern="did:plc:.+" /></label>
          <label>Handle<input name="handle" /></label>
          <label>Managed PDS URL<input name="pdsUrl" required defaultValue="https://pds.notorganic.info" /></label>
          <label>Product account ID<input name="productAccountId" required /></label>
          <button type="submit">Redeem invite</button>
          <output>{invite.message}</output>
        </form>
      </Panel>

      <Panel eyebrow="Account access" title="Complete recovery">
        <form onSubmit={recover}>
          <label>Recovery challenge<input name="challengeHash" required /></label>
          <label>New PDS URL<input name="newPdsUrl" type="url" required /></label>
          <button type="submit">Recover account</button>
          <output>{recovery.message}</output>
        </form>
      </Panel>

      <Panel eyebrow="Your data" title="Portable by default">
        <p>Export your identity mapping, wallet ledger, grants, inference history, subscription, and consent records as JSON.</p>
        <button onClick={() => void deletion.run(exportData, "Export downloaded.")}>Download export</button>
        <output>{deletion.message}</output>
      </Panel>

      <Panel eyebrow="Danger zone" title="Two systems, two decisions">
        <p>Deleting provider data does not delete your ATProto repository. Deleting the managed PDS account does not erase retained billing audit records.</p>
        <DeletionButton scope="provider" phrase="DELETE PROVIDER DATA" operation={deletion} />
        <DeletionButton scope="pds" phrase="DELETE PDS ACCOUNT" operation={deletion} />
      </Panel>
    </div>
  );
}

